 We then have

	  \begin{alignedat}{3}
	  A\vec{x}\amp{}={}\amp -9\vec{v_1} \amp{}-{}\amp 4\vec{v_2}\\
	  A^2\vec{x}\amp{}={}\amp -27\vec{v_1}\amp{}+{}\amp8\vec{v_2} \\
	  A^{-1}\vec{x}\amp{}={}\amp -\vec{v_1} \amp{}-{}\amp \vec{v_2}\text{.} \\
	  \end{alignedat}

 We find

	  \begin{alignedat}{3}
	  A\vec{x}\amp{}={}\amp -9\vec{v_1} \amp{}-{}\amp 4\vec{v_2}\\
	  A^2\vec{x}\amp{}={}\amp -27\vec{v_1}\amp{}+{}\amp8\vec{v_2} \\
	  A^{-1}\vec{x}\amp{}={}\amp -\vec{v_1} \amp{}-{}\amp \vec{v_2}\text{.} \\
	  \end{alignedat}

From the results of the previous part, we have
A = \begin{bmatrix}
1 \amp 2 \\
2 \amp -2 \\
\end{bmatrix}
.

